{title: Take My Life, and Let It Be}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{columns: 2}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C]Take my [**]life, and [F]let it [G]be
[C]Consec[Am]rated, [C]Lord, to [G]thee
[C]Take my [**]moments [F]and my [G]days
[C]Let them [**]flow in [G]ceaseless [C]praise
[G]Take my [Dm]hands, and [Em]let them [C]move
[G]At the [Dm]impulse [G]of thy [C]love
[C]Take my [**]feet, and [F]let them [G]be
[C]Swift and [**]beauti[G]ful for [C]thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C]Take my [**]voice, and [F]let me [G]sing
[C]Always, [Am]only, [C]for my [G]King
[C]Take my [**]lips, and [F]let them [G]be
[C]Filled with [**]messa[G]ges from [C]thee
[G]Take my [Dm]silver [Em]and my [C]gold
[G]Not a [Dm]mite would [G]I with[C]hold
[C]Take my [**]intel[F]lect, and [G]use
[C]Every [**]power as [G]thou shalt [C]choose.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C]Take my [**]will, and [F]make it [G]thine
[C]It shall [Am]be no [C]longer [G]mine
[C]Take my [**]heart, it [F]is thine [G]own
[C]It shall [**]be thy [G]royal [C]throne
[G]Take my [Dm]love, my [Em]Lord, I [C]pour
[G]At thy [Dm]feet its [G]treasure-[C]store
[C]Take my[**]self, and [F]I will [G]be
[C]Ever, [**]only, [G]all for [C]thee.
{end_of_verse}
